    "name": "choice",
    "text": "<p>When the array is empty, the line <code>result += strs[strs.length - 1];</code> runs with <code>strs.length</code> equal to <code>0</code>. That produces the index <code>-1</code> for the array lookup, which produces the error. The body of the method doesn’t work for empty arrays! We could try to re-work the logic around this case. We could also just add a single line at the beginning. Think about this! What line of code could we add at the beginning to return the empty string if the array is empty?</p>\n\n<p><iframe height=\"1000px\" scrolling=\"yes\" src=\"https://tech.io/playground-widget/90c00bc69c16a6fd595d970b9971ad8c20785/welcome/1091596/Intersperse\" width=\"100%\"></iframe></p>\n\n<h3><span style=\"color: #cc0000;\">Do Now!</span> Which of the following lines, when added to the beginning of the method, will make all the tests pass? Choose all that apply.</h3>",
